<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">3. UI/UX Conside=
rations</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Debounced Visual Updates=
:</strong>
For rapidly changing data like stock prices, I implement visual debouncing =
where the actual value updates immediately (for calculations) but the displ=
ayed value updates at a human-readable rate.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Priority-Based Updates:<=
/strong>
Not all data needs real-time updates. Account balances might update every f=
ew seconds, while active trading positions need millisecond precision.</p>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">4. Performance M=
onitoring</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I always implement <strong>perfo=
rmance budgets</strong> and monitoring:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Frame rate monitoring to ensure=
 smooth interactions</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Memory usage tracking to preven=
t leaks from WebSocket subscriptions</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Bundle size analysis to keep th=
e application lean</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The key insight</strong>=
 I've learned is that real-time doesn't always mean instant visual updates =
- it's about providing the right data at the right frequency for the user's=
 current context.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Im=
pressive! I can tell you've dealt with these challenges in production. Now,=
 let's transition to a more hands-on problem. We often need to compare comp=
lex data structures for audit trails, change detection, and synchronization=
 purposes. I'm going to give you a coding challenge that we've actually fac=
ed in our transaction processing system.</p>
<hr>
