<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Additional optimizations=
:</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Streaming comparison</s=
trong> for very large objects</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Worker threads</strong>=
 for CPU-intensive comparisons</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Lazy evaluation</strong=
> - only compute differences when accessed</li>
</ul>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">3. Array Compari=
son Design Decision</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I chose to treat arrays as <stro=
ng>atomic values</strong> rather than element-by-element comparison for sev=
eral reasons:</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5"><strong>Semantic=
 Reasoning:</strong></h3>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">In most business contexts, espec=
ially banking, arrays often represent <strong>complete datasets</strong> wh=
ere the order and completeness matter more than individual element changes.=
 For example:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Account permissions</st=
rong>: <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 tex=
t-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]"=
>["read", "write"]</code> vs <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5=
 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-=
1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">["read"]</code> should be treated as a complete chan=
ge</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Transaction categories<=
/strong>: The entire list represents a state, not individual items</li>
</ul>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5"><strong>Performa=
nce Considerations:</strong></h3>
