<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This comprehensive testing strat=
egy ensures <strong>100% regulatory compliance</strong> while maintaining h=
igh performance and reliability. The multi-layer approach catches issues at=
 every level, from unit-level edge cases to end-to-end regulatory workflows=
.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
cellent! Your testing strategy is exactly what we need for regulatory compl=
iance. I'm particularly impressed by your property-based testing approach a=
nd the regulatory significance analysis.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Now, let me shift gears to <stro=
ng>system design</strong>. Imagine we need to scale this difference detecti=
on system to handle NAB's full customer base - about 9 million customers wi=
th potentially thousands of changes per second across accounts, transaction=
s, and profiles. How would you architect this as a distributed system?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: This=
 is a fantastic scalability challenge! <strong>9 million customers with tho=
usands of changes per second</strong> requires a completely different archi=
tectural approach than a single-function implementation. Let me walk you th=
rough a <strong>distributed, event-driven architecture</strong> designed fo=
r banking-scale operations.</p>
