<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5"><strong>Key Arch=
itecture Benefits:</strong></h2>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Horizontal Scalability<=
/strong>: Can handle 9M+ customers by adding more workers</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Event-Driven</strong>: =
Processes changes as they happen, no batch delays</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Fault Tolerance</strong=
>: Worker failures don't affect the system</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Regulatory Compliance</=
strong>: Built-in audit trails and compliance reporting</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance Optimizatio=
n</strong>: Specialized handling for different change types</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Real-time Analytics</st=
rong>: Immediate insights into change patterns</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Cost Efficiency</strong=
>: Scales down during low-traffic periods</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This architecture can easily han=
dle <strong>10,000+ changes per second</strong> while maintaining <strong>s=
ub-second response times</strong> for query operations and ensuring <strong=
>100% audit trail accuracy</strong> for regulatory compliance.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ou=
tstanding system design! Your event-driven architecture and the considerati=
on for regulatory compliance really shows enterprise-level thinking. The ho=
rizontal scaling strategy and specialized worker types are exactly what we'=
d need at NAB's scale.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me ask you one final challen=
ging question that combines both technical depth and business acumen: <stro=
ng>How would you handle a scenario where we discover that our difference de=
tection system has been missing certain types of changes for the past 6 mon=
ths due to a bug, and we now need to reprocess 50 million historical record=
s to ensure regulatory compliance?</strong> This is unfortunately a real sc=
enario that can happen in banking systems.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: This=
 is an excellent question that touches on <strong>data integrity, regulator=
y compliance, and crisis management</strong> - all critical aspects of bank=
ing operations. A <strong>6-month data gap affecting 50 million records</st=
rong> is exactly the kind of scenario that requires both technical excellen=
ce and strategic thinking.</p>
